Health: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines health check model beyond simple 200 OK.

HealthLevels:
  Liveness: Service is running, process alive
  Readiness: Service can accept traffic, dependencies available
  DependencyHealth: Downstream dependencies are healthy

HealthCheck:
  Required:
    Liveness: Always
    Readiness: Always for production
    Dependency: For services with external dependencies

Response:
  Healthy: status healthy, checks OK
  Degraded: status degraded, dependencies DEGRADED
  Unhealthy: status unhealthy, checks FAIL

Rules:
  [HL1] Health endpoints MUST be protected.
  [HL2] Liveness failure triggers restart.
  [HL3] Readiness failure removes from load balancer.
  [HL4] Dependency failure marks service as degraded.

State: +
